1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:08,840
Hold on, hold on. Before you eat today, listen as these Native Americans describe in full detail the true history of Thanksgiving.

2
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:15,620
Happy Thanksgiving, America. I'm Donette, and I'm here with my friends to tell you the real history behind this holiday.

3
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,960
Growing up, I knew that what they told you in school about Thanksgiving wasn't true.

4
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:23,460
That's not the true story.

5
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:32,740
The true story behind Thanksgiving was, after every killing of a whole village, these European settlers celebrated it, and they called it Thanksgiving.

6
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:37,960
But it wasn't until Abraham Lincoln became president that it became an official holiday.

7
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:44,960
He ordered 38 Dakota men to be hung for war crimes after the sacred holiday Christmas.

8
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:53,780
We take this time to remember our elders who lost their lives due to what really happened.

9
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:59,340
Usually, my mom makes a Native American dish for us, and we pray.

10
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:03,540
Growing up, I would be kind of annoyed that they didn't know what actually happened on Thanksgiving,

11
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:09,080
and that they're actually celebrating the deaths of many people and many tribes that were lost.

12
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:17,180
Whether it's to give thanks, or to be with your family, you shouldn't learn how that holiday was established in the first place.

13
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:20,980
I'm thankful for being born Indigenous to this continent.

14
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,700
I'm thankful that I still have my culture.

15
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:28,240
I'm thankful that my elders kept our culture alive all these years.

16
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:32,800
I'm thankful to be Indigenous, resilient, and alive.

17
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:38,940
I'm thankful for us all to be able to stand together, stand strong, and stand as one.

18
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,140
Happy Thanksgiving, America.

19
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:47,340
Let me know in the comments, what does this day mean to you?

20
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:48,680
Do you acknowledge it?

21
00:01:49,160 --> 00:01:50,200
Do you celebrate it?

22
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:52,860
What do your kids know or think about it?

23
00:01:52,860 --> 00:02:10,860
Do you Father?

24
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,740
Do you know how good it is?

25
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,400
Do you practice it?

26
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:16,500
I'll do you.

27
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:17,940
I'll do you.

